     "text": "**CLINICAL SUMMARY - Williamson-Miller Medical Group**\n\n**Patient:** Chase Rice \n**DOB:** 03/11/1970 \n**Sex:** M \n**MRN:** 224687\n\n---\n\n**Encounters:**\n\n- **2025-02-13:** The patient presented for follow-up regarding their Transient Ischemic Attack (TIA) which occurred approximately years ago. The patient reports no recent episodes of transient neurological deficits. The blood pressure was 112/67 mmHg and weight was 104 lb.\n- **2024-07-07:** The patient visited for a flu shot. There were no acute complaints at the time of the visit. The blood pressure was 116/63 mmHg and weight was 118 lb.\n- **2023-11-29:** The patient returned for a follow-up visit regarding a No recent episodes of transient neurological symptoms were reported. The blood pressure was 121/61 mmHg and weight was 108 lb.\n- **2023-04-22:** The patient came in for a TIA follow-up. The patient reported no new episodes since the previous visit. Blood pressure was 111/67 mmHg and weight was 117 lb.\n- **2022-09-13:** The patient presented with symptoms of a TIA. The episode was controlled with no further incidents reported since then. The blood pressure was 112/67 mmHg and weight was 108 lb.\n- **2022-02-04:** The patient visited for a follow-up regarding a TIA that had occurred. There were no new episodes reported. Blood pressure was 112/63 mmHg and weight was 114 lb.\n- **2021-06-28:** The patient came in due to a back strain. There no neurological symptoms reported. Blood pressure was 113/62 mmHg and weight was 107 lb.\n\n---\n\n**Assessment/Plan:**\n\n- **TIA (0.7 years - controlled:** The patient has been stable since their last TIA, which occurred approximately 0.7 years ago. There have been no reported episodes of transient neurological deficits since the last visit. Currently, the patient is not on any medications for this condition.\n \n**Social History:**\n\n- The patient reports consuming approximately four alcoholic drinks per week.\n\n---\n\n**Additional Findings:**\n\n- **Physical Examination:** \n - General: The patient appears well, in no acute distress.\n - Cardiovascular: Heart rate regular, no murmurs.\n - Neurological: No focal deficits, cranial nerves intact.\n - Musculoskeletal: No tenderness, full range of motion.\n\n- **Vitals:** \n - Blood Pressure: 112/67 mmHg\n - Weight: 104 lb\n\n---\n\n**Additional Patient Information:**\n\n- **Family History:** The patient's father had hypertension and passed away at the age of 77. There are no other significant family medical histories reported.\n\n- **Lifestyle:** The patient reports a generally healthy lifestyle. He denies smoking and"
